selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#submodules\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Submodules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#submodules\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"constants/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.constants<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.constants\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Attributes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#attributes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"impeller/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.impeller<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.impeller\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Preliminary radial impeller sizing and physical inputs for pyTurbo Aero.</p><p>No surface generator or efficiency predictor is run during construction.\nMetal angles are measured from the backward circumferential direction toward\nthe meridional direction. Positive wrap denotes backward sweep for +x rotation.</p>", "a[href=\"pump_cli/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.pump_cli<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.pump_cli\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Command-line preliminary impeller sizing, with explicit design inputs.</p>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Preliminary centrifugal pump design with optional pyTurbo blade generation.</p>", "a[href=\"duty/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.duty<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.duty\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>The duty a pump is designed for: flow, head and speed.</p><p>A pump is usually specified as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Q</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">H</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></code>, but in an engine those\nfall out of a medium, a mass flow and two pressures. <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"duty/PumpDuty.html#pyskyfire.pump.duty.PumpDuty\" title=\"pyskyfire.pump.duty.PumpDuty\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PumpDuty</span></code></a> takes\neither and stores the same thing, so a design reads it the same way whichever\nthe user had to hand.</p>", "a[href=\"disk_friction/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.disk_friction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.disk_friction\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Friction on the outside of a spinning impeller: its disk friction loss.</p><p>A shrouded impeller\u2019s two outer faces turn in the fluid filling the gaps\nbetween them and the casing. The shear on them costs shaft power and heats the\nfluid. The flow through the blades never sees any of it, so it is charged here,\nnot in the hydraulic efficiency.</p>", "a[href=\"utils/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.utils<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.utils\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"_pyturbo/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump._pyturbo<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump._pyturbo\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Translate physical pump inputs to pyTurbo 1.3.8 construction controls.</p><p>The conformal (m\u2019,theta) plane uses dm\u2019=dm/r. Metal angles are from +m\u2019,\nand upstream wrap_angle means atan(dtheta/m\u2019), not total blade wrap.\nThickness controls are section-normal offsets in this plane: locally t/(2r).</p>", "a[href=\"diffuser/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.diffuser\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Vaned radial diffuser between an impeller and its volute.</p><p>A vaneless volute collects the impeller discharge at nearly the speed it left\nthe wheel, and it carries it round the whole circumference that way, so its\nfriction is paid at the impeller\u2019s own dynamic head. Vanes take the swirl out\nsooner. They are fixed, so they do no work: they push on the flow, remove its\nangular momentum and turn it outward, so it reaches the volute radius in a\nshort path, and the channels between them widen, so it slows by their area\nratio rather than only by the radius ratio. The volute behind then collects\nslow, low-swirl flow.</p>", "a[href=\"geometry/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.geometry<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.geometry\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Pump geometry contracts. Lengths are metres; cylindrical arrays are (x,r,theta).</p><p>The shaft is +x, and which way it turns about that axis is named by the\nimpeller\u2019s <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></code>: counterclockwise means the right-handed sense about\n+x, seen with the axis pointing at the viewer. A backward-swept blade has\ndecreasing theta from leading to trailing edge in that sense, and a clockwise\nimpeller is its mirror image, built by negating theta.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
